{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "1586d5d3-3889-882f-91ba-2d80118a0a54",
  "created_at": "2026-02-03T10:47:27-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Omar Mensah",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:43:37-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:43:42-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, good morning. Omar Mensah here. I own a two-family place, I rent out both sides. And I've got a situation with the fence between my lot and the neighbor's."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:43:53-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. What's going on with the fence?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:43:56-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, we don't agree on whose it is. He says it's mine, I say it's his, and it's leaning pretty good now, toward his side. Back in the nineties, when I first bought, the fella before me had a dog, and that fence was, ah, sorry. I'm wandering. Anyway, nobody knows who's supposed to fix it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:44:16-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine. Let me ask a few things so I point you right. Is the fence right on the property line, or is it set back on one side?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:44:27-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right about on the line, I'd say. I never had a survey done that I can find. The posts are on my side of the grass, though, or I think they are. He thinks they're on his."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:44:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And has anyone put anything in writing, like a letter from him, or a notice to you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:44:47-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just a note in my mailbox. It said the fence was my responsibility and to take care of it. No signature."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:44:55-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. So here's the thing. Who owns a fence and who has to maintain it is generally a matter between the two property owners. It's not something our office decides. What we can do is look at it if it's a safety problem or a code issue on the city side."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:45:14-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, right. So who do I talk to about it? I'd like to sit down with somebody. Is there a city council I can bring it to? Or I figure I'd want to get council for myself, too, somebody to advise me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:45:29-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just so I'm clear, are you asking about the City Council, the elected body? Or someone who gives you advice, like legal counsel?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:45:38-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Counsel, yes, the advice kind. I mix those up every time. My daughter used to tease me about that. Sorry, there I go again. Yes, counsel."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:45:48-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. For that, I'd suggest a private attorney or the state bar's referral service, since the city can't advise you on a dispute between neighbors. The City Council doesn't settle these either. If you want, I can also tell you what a survey would involve."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:46:04-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. That seems like step one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:46:07-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A licensed land surveyor can mark the actual boundary. Once you know where the line is, you'll know whose land the posts are on, and that usually settles most of it. Some people also try mediation if they can't agree, and there are community mediation programs in the state."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:46:24-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mediation. Okay. Write that down. And does your office need to know anything? Like, should I tell you the fence is leaning?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:46:32-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If it's leaning into a sidewalk or a street, or it looks like it could fall and hurt someone, yes, report that and an inspector can take a look. If it's just between your two yards, it's mostly a civil matter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:46:47-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's just between the yards. Maybe a foot of lean. The tenants' kids don't play back there much, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:46:55-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Then I'd start with the survey, and try talking to him again once you have the line marked. If anything changes, or it starts to come down, call us back and we'll send someone."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:47:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's helpful. Survey, then mediation, and a private counsel if it goes sideways. Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:47:15-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it exactly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:47:17-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Thank you, Anita. That's what I needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:47:21-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mr. Mensah. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-03T10:47:25-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too."
    }
  ],
